 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "EventLogger(window) sets the cooldown. logEvent(name, timestamp) is called with non-decreasing timestamps. It prints (returns true) when the name was never printed or timestamp - (time the name was last printed) >= window, and then records timestamp as that name's last print time; otherwise it returns false and records nothing. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
